<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conradin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1252">1252</a>–<a href="/years/1268">1268</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Conrad III of Jerusalem, Conrad V of Swabia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conradin was the last legitimate member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen dynasty</a>, Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia">Swabia</a> and claimant to the kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. At fifteen he invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to recover Sicily from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a>, but was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tagliacozzo">Battle of Tagliacozzo</a> in 1268. Captured while fleeing, he was beheaded in the market square of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> on 29 October 1268.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conradin.jpg" alt="Conradin" width="320" height="462" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Konradin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
